Frequently Asked Interview Questions
------------------------------------

Q. What is High Cohesion?

A:
"High cohesion means a class has one well-defined responsibility,
and all its methods and data are closely related to that responsibility."

--------------------------------------------------

Q. Why is High Cohesion important?

A:
• Easier maintenance
• Better readability
• Easier testing
• Better reusability
• Fewer bugs
• Localized changes

--------------------------------------------------

Q. Difference between High Cohesion and Low Coupling?

A:
High Cohesion focuses on keeping related functionality together within a class,
while Low Coupling focuses on minimizing dependencies between different classes.

--------------------------------------------------

Q. Is High Cohesion related to SRP?

A:
Yes. A class following the Single Responsibility Principle usually has
High Cohesion because it focuses on one responsibility.

--------------------------------------------------

One-Line Definition
-------------------

"High Cohesion means designing a class so that all its methods and data are
closely related and work together to fulfill one well-defined responsibility."
